FFmpeg
Project: https://ffmpeg.org/
Licensing information: https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

F10 Recorder launches FFmpeg as a separate executable for capture, encoding,
segmentation, screenshots, and MP4 export. A compatible existing installation
is reused without modification. Otherwise, the Windows prototype downloads:

Package: ffmpeg-9.0.2-essentials_build.zip, supplied by Gyan
URL: https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/packages/ffmpeg-9.0.2-essentials_build.zip
SHA-256: 60f467265b1e312373dbcd92200c2618a74850f98d3d078e94296bb3fa2047ba
Build information: https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/

This exact fallback build reports GNU GPL version 3 or later through
ffmpeg -L. It enables GPL components and version 3. Its upstream LICENSE,
README.txt, documentation, and presets are retained alongside the private
binary under the user's F10Recorder/runtime installation directory.
GNU GPL version 3: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

Other compatible existing builds can have different licenses and build flags.
FFmpeg is generally LGPL, but optional GPL components change the license of
the resulting FFmpeg build. Do not describe this fallback build as LGPL.

